<title>USA: Conde Nast vice president to retire.</title>
<headline>Conde Nast vice president to retire.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Magazine publishing firm Conde Nast said on Thursday that Joseph Fuchs will retire as vice president after 38 years with the company, effective December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>Michael Clinton, senior vice president for group sales, will become executive vice president on October 1, 1996, the company said. Mademoiselle publisher Catherine Viscardi Johnston will take Clinton's position as senior vice president.</p>
<p>Fuchs will continue to serve as a consultant to the company.</p>
</text>
